(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRewritingSystem", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"f9bea772-9ac3-1c4a-9304-9ed79d834022"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRewritingSystem", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rules", ",", " ", "init"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5e9659dd-6cc0-6946-afa0-49c424ea089b"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewriting system with the given rules started from the \
hypergraph init."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"dcba498b-bf35-6342-92ec-ed0dfc453c90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"sys", "[", 
    RowBox[{"prop", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"23878830-af8a-9f4b-b488-5da3efd65df3"],
 " ",
 "gives a property of the evolution carried n generations."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"8ec4e77f-2524-8a42-8276-c7052be4143c"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"f9e8d77e-f23b-8347-b009-7d42481a944b"],

Cell["\<\
rules may be one HypergraphRule, a list of them, or plain arrows input -> \
output, which are converted; init may be anything Hypergraph accepts.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a3967ea9-3fc3-e446-86a8-9ac31cf22d71"],

Cell["\<\
Evolving means applying every rule in every way it fits, to every state \
reached so far. The result is a tree of state occurrences joined by events: a \
state reached two ways appears twice, since which elements it is made of \
depends on how it was reached.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c99f402d-c8a7-f24e-9618-e348eeb4b568"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The properties are \"Rules\", \"RuleCount\", \"InitialState\", \"States\", \
\"StateList\", \"StateCount\", \"EventList\", \"EventCount\", \
\"EvolutionGraph\", \"StatesGraph\", \"BranchialGraph\", \"CausalGraph\", \
\"CausalEdges\" and \"EvolutionCausalGraph\". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"sys", "[", "\"\<Properties\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"185247ab-a681-8d4a-82fe-0cc1a6bebc39"],
 " lists them."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"49c939fe-7112-7a40-8314-0fff94508d9c"],

Cell["\<\
The number of generations defaults to 1, so sys[\"CausalGraph\"] and \
sys[\"CausalGraph\", 1] are the same.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e640a96c-4b8b-9c44-ae27-2c00b5198831"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Options are those of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphCausalGraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a53ee175-12e5-fb4e-9ac2-600050894887"],
 ", and are given to the property: \"CausalDependence\", \
\"TransitiveReduction\", \"CanonicalizeStates\", \"MaxStates\", and the \
matching options \"Labeled\", \"LabelPatterns\" and \"DistinctVertices\"."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4a4f2524-1876-6d4c-897f-daf6059057b1"],

Cell["\<\
An event of \"EventList\" is an association with \"Rule\" and \"RuleIndex\", \
which rule fired; \"Generation\"; \"InputState\" and \"OutputState\", indices \
into \"StateList\"; \"ConsumedEdges\", \"CreatedEdges\", \"MatchedVertices\", \
\"CreatedVertices\" and \"DestroyedVertices\", the elements it touched, as \
tokens; and \"Data\", the event HypergraphRuleApply gave.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fe877e62-2733-a34d-8cb7-72b1e15cba4a"],

Cell["\<\
Elements are tracked by token rather than by value, because an edge is an \
element of a multiset: two edges that look the same are still two elements, \
and a vertex identifier freed by one event may be handed out again by a later \
one. A token is minted when an element is created and carried for as long as \
it survives.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6d6bef83-2018-874d-b7ee-d9c500cf8114"],

Cell["\<\
\"MaxStates\", by default 2048, stops an evolution that is growing faster \
than expected and gives HypergraphRewritingSystem::trunc rather than running \
on.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4f72d503-2bb2-5243-90a1-d356c8ff6077"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"355c8d01-58e7-4f40-b7ff-2bd136641076"],

Cell["A rule that subdivides an edge, started from one edge:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"e0a740b7-56a2-d141-a97c-8e8f13a36f07"],

Cell["\<\
subdivide = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}];
system = HypergraphRewritingSystem[subdivide, Hypergraph[{{1, 2}}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a2afd2f9-616b-5e49-bfd6-5fd14814e05c"],

